[40.669472, "o", "ð¬ [security]: # Security Best Practices Summary\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð Authentication & Authorization\r\r\n\r\r\n### Authentication\r\r\n- **Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)**: Implement for all critical systems and admin accounts\r\r\n- **Strong Password Policies**: Enforce minimum 12+ characters, complexity requirements, password rotation\r\r\n- **Session Management**: \r\r\n  - Use secure, randomly generated session tokens\r\r\n  - Implement proper session timeout (15-30 min for sensitive apps)\r\r\n  - Invalidate sessions on logout and password changes\r\r\n  - Use `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, and `SameSite` flags on cookies\r\r\n- **Password Storage**: Use bcrypt, Argon2, or scrypt with proper salt and work factors\r\r\n- **Account Lockout**: Implement rate limiting and temporary lockouts after failed attempts\r\r\n\r\r\n### Authorization\r\r\n- **Principle of Least Privilege**: Grant minimum necessary permissions\r\r\n- **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**: Implement granular permission systems\r\r\n- **Verify Authorization**: Check permissions on **every"]
[40.669487, "o", "** request, never trust cl"]
[40.669546, "o", "ient-side validation\r\r\n- **Object-Level Authorization**: Verify user access to specific resources, not just endpoints\r\r\n- **Avoid Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA)**: Never expose sequential/guessable IDs without authorization checks\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð¡️ Injection Prevention\r\r\n\r\r\n### SQL Injection\r\r\n- **Use Parameterized Queries**: Never concatenate user input into SQL\r\r\n- **ORM/Query Builders**: Use prepared statements and parameter binding\r\r\n- **Input Validation**: Whitelist acceptable characters and patterns\r\r\n- **Least Privilege DB Users**: Application should use limited-permission database accounts\r\r\n\r\r\n### Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)\r\r\n- **Output Encoding**: Escape all user-generated content in HTML, JS, CSS contexts\r\r\n- **Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Implement strict CSP headers\r\r\n- **Sanitization Libraries**: Use well-tested libraries (DOMPurify, OWASP Java Encoder)\r\r\n- **Avoid `innerHTML`**: Use safer DOM manipulation methods\r\r\n\r\r\n### Command Injection\r\r\n- **Avoid Shell Execution**:"]
[40.669558, "o", " Use language-native libr"]
[40.669625, "o", "aries instead of shell commands\r\r\n- **Input Validation**: Strictly validate and sanitize all parameters\r\r\n- **Whitelist Approach**: Only allow known-safe commands/arguments\r\r\n\r\r\n### Other Injections\r\r\n- **LDAP, XML, XPath**: Use parameterized interfaces\r\r\n- **Template Injection**: Sandbox template engines, validate user input\r\r\n- **Log Injection**: Sanitize data before logging to prevent log forging\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð Secrets & Credential Management\r\r\n\r\r\n### Storage\r\r\n- **Never Hardcode Secrets**: No credentials, API keys, or tokens in source code\r\r\n- **Environment Variables**: Use for configuration, but not the only layer\r\r\n- **Secrets Management**: Use HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, or similar\r\r\n- **Encryption at Rest**: Encrypt sensitive configuration files and databases\r\r\n\r\r\n### Exposure Prevention\r\r\n- **`.gitignore`**: Exclude `.env`, config files, credentials from version control\r\r\n- **Secret Scanning**: Use tools like GitGuardian, TruffleHog, or GitHub Secret Scanning\r\r\n-"]
[40.669642, "o", " **Rotate Regularly**: Imp"]
[40.669701, "o", "lement automatic rotation for API keys, tokens, certificates\r\r\n- **Separate Environments**: Different credentials for dev/staging/production\r\r\n\r\r\n### Transmission\r\r\n- **TLS/HTTPS Only**: Encrypt all data in transit\r\r\n- **API Key Headers**: Never pass secrets in URLs (use headers or POST body)\r\r\n- **Short-Lived Tokens**: Implement token expiration and refresh mechanisms\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð¦ Dependency & Supply Chain Security\r\r\n\r\r\n### Dependency Management\r\r\n- **Keep Dependencies Updated**: Regularly update to patch known vulnerabilities\r\r\n- **Automated Scanning**: Use Dependabot, Snyk, OWASP Dependency-Check, or `npm audit`\r\r\n- **Minimal Dependencies**: Apply the \"2-3× value\" rule—fewer dependencies = smaller attack surface\r\r\n- **Lock Files**: Use `package-lock.json`, `Pipfile.lock`, `go.sum` to ensure reproducible builds\r\r\n- **Verify Integrity**: Use SRI (Subresource Integrity) for CDN resources\r\r\n\r\r\n### Supply Chain Attacks\r\r\n- **Source Verification**: Only use packages from trusted registries\r\r\n- **"]
[40.669708, "o", "Package Signing**: Verify"]
[40.669782, "o", " signatures when available\r\r\n- **Dependency Reviews**: Audit new dependencies before adoption\r\r\n- **Private Registry**: Consider mirroring critical dependencies internally\r\r\n\r\r\n### Vulnerability Response\r\r\n- **Severity Assessment**: Prioritize critical/high severity CVEs\r\r\n- **Patch Testing**: Test updates in staging before production deployment\r\r\n- **Emergency Process**: Have a rapid-response plan for zero-day vulnerabilities\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð API Security\r\r\n\r\r\n### Authentication & Rate Limiting\r\r\n- **API Keys/Tokens**: Use OAuth 2.0, JWT, or API keys with proper scoping\r\r\n- **Rate Limiting**: Implement per-user/IP rate limits to prevent abuse\r\r\n- **Throttling**: Use exponential backoff for repeated failures\r\r\n- **IP Whitelisting**: For sensitive APIs, restrict access by IP when possible\r\r\n\r\r\n### Input Validation & Output Handling\r\r\n- **Schema Validation**: Validate all input against strict schemas (JSON Schema, OpenAPI)\r\r\n- **Size Limits**: Enforce max payload sizes to prevent DoS\r\r\n- **Content-Type"]
[40.669791, "o", " Validation**: Verify `Con"]
[40.669868, "o", "tent-Type` headers match payload\r\r\n- **Error Messages**: Don't expose stack traces or internal details in responses\r\r\n\r\r\n### CORS & Headers\r\r\n- **CORS Policy**: Restrict allowed origins, avoid wildcards in production\r\r\n- **Security Headers**: \r\r\n  - `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`\r\r\n  - `X-Frame-Options: DENY` or `SAMEORIGIN`\r\r\n  - `Strict-Transport-Security` (HSTS)\r\r\n  - `X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block`\r\r\n\r\r\n### Versioning & Deprecation\r\r\n- **API Versioning**: Use versioned endpoints to safely introduce breaking changes\r\r\n- **Deprecation Notices**: Give users advance warning before removing functionality\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð Monitoring & Incident Response\r\r\n\r\r\n### Logging & Monitoring\r\r\n- **Security Event Logging**: Log authentication attempts, authorization failures, suspicious activities\r\r\n- **Log Sanitization**: Prevent injection attacks in logs (strip newlines, control characters)\r\r\n- **Centralized Logging**: Use SIEM systems for aggregation and analysis\r\r\n- **Alerting**: Set up alerts for anomal"]
[40.669876, "o", "ous patterns (multiple fail"]
[40.669942, "o", "ed logins, privilege escalations)\r\r\n\r\r\n### Incident Response\r\r\n- **Incident Response Plan**: Document procedures for security breaches\r\r\n- **Regular Drills**: Practice response scenarios quarterly\r\r\n- **Forensics Capability**: Maintain logs and backups for post-incident analysis\r\r\n- **Communication Plan**: Have templates for notifying users/stakeholders\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n## ✅ General Security Principles\r\r\n\r\r\n1. **Defense in Depth**: Multiple layers of security controls\r\r\n2. **Fail Securely**: Default to deny access when errors occur\r\r\n3. **Security by Design**: Integrate security from project inception\r\r\n4. **Regular Audits**: Conduct code reviews and security assessments\r\r\n5. **Security Training**: Keep team updated on OWASP Top 10 and current threats\r\r\n6. **Patch Management**: Apply security updates within 24-48 hours for critical issues\r\r\n7. **Backup & Recovery**: Regular encrypted backups, tested restore procedures\r\r\n8. **Compliance**: Follow relevant standards (PCI DSS, HIPAA, GDPR, SOC 2)\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n##"]
[40.669946, "o", " ð¨ Severity Levels R"]
[40.670018, "o", "eference\r\r\n\r\r\n- **CRITICAL**: Immediate exploitation possible, full system compromise\r\r\n- **HIGH**: Significant risk, requires urgent patching (within 7 days)\r\r\n- **MEDIUM**: Moderate risk, patch within 30 days\r\r\n- **LOW**: Minimal immediate risk, address in regular maintenance cycles\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n> **Remember**: Security is **not a feature**, it's a **fundamental requirement**.  \r\r\n> Build it in from day one, maintain it continuously, and never compromise on the basics.\r\r\n"]
