[71.108224, "o", "ð¬ [docs]: # What Makes Good Documentation\r\r\n\r\r\nGood documentation is essential for the success and longevity of any software project. Here are the key principles:\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð¯ Core Principles\r\r\n\r\r\n### 1. **Clarity and Simplicity**\r\r\n- Use plain language and avoid unnecessary jargon\r\r\n- Explain complex concepts in progressively detailed layers\r\r\n- One concept per section—avoid cognitive overload\r\r\n- Short paragraphs and sentences for scannability\r\r\n\r\r\n### 2. **Completeness Without Verbosity**\r\r\n- Cover all necessary aspects of the topic\r\r\n- Provide enough context for understanding\r\r\n- Avoid redundancy and filler content\r\r\n- Balance thoroughness with conciseness\r\r\n\r\r\n### 3. **Structure and Organization**\r\r\n- Clear hierarchy with logical headings (H1 → H2 → H3)\r\r\n- Consistent formatting throughout\r\r\n- Table of contents for longer documents\r\r\n- Progressive disclosure: overview → details → advanced topics\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð Essential Components\r\r\n\r\r\n### **README Files**\r\r\nShould answer these que"]
[71.108229, "o", "stions in order:\r\r\n1. **What** is this p"]
[71.108285, "o", "roject?\r\r\n2. **Why** does it exist? (Problem it solves)\r\r\n3. **How** do I install/use it? (Quick start)\r\r\n4. **Where** can I learn more? (Links to detailed docs)\r\r\n\r\r\n### **API Documentation**\r\r\n- **Function signatures** with parameter types\r\r\n- **Purpose**: What does it do?\r\r\n- **Parameters**: Name, type, description, required/optional\r\r\n- **Return values**: Type and meaning\r\r\n- **Examples**: Real-world usage patterns\r\r\n- **Error cases**: What can go wrong and why\r\r\n\r\r\n### **Code Comments**\r\r\n- Explain **why**, not **what** (code shows what)\r\r\n- Document non-obvious decisions\r\r\n- Warn about gotchas or edge cases\r\r\n- Keep them up-to-date with code changes\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð¡ Best Practices\r\r\n\r\r\n### **Examples Are Essential**\r\r\n```go\r\r\n// ❌ Bad: No example\r\r\n// ProcessData processes the input data\r\r\nfunc ProcessData(ctx context.Context, data []byte) error\r\r\n\r\r\n// ✅ Good: With example\r\r\n// ProcessData validates and transforms raw input data.\r\r\n//\r\r\n// Example:\r\r\n//   data := []byte(`{\"name\": \"test\"}`)\r\r\n//   i"]
[71.108301, "o", "f err := ProcessData(ctx, data); err"]
[71.108379, "o", " != nil {\r\r\n//       log.Fatal(err)\r\r\n//   }\r\r\nfunc ProcessData(ctx context.Context, data []byte) error\r\r\n```\r\r\n\r\r\n### **Progressive Depth**\r\r\n- **Quick Start**: 5 minutes to working code\r\r\n- **Tutorial**: 30 minutes to understand core concepts\r\r\n- **Guide**: Deep dive into specific features\r\r\n- **Reference**: Complete API/configuration details\r\r\n\r\r\n### **Maintainability**\r\r\n- Documentation lives close to code (reduces drift)\r\r\n- Automated generation where possible (OpenAPI, godoc, JSDoc)\r\r\n- Use dynamic help menus (e.g., `just --list`) instead of static lists\r\r\n- Version documentation with the code\r\r\n\r\r\n### **User-Centric Focus**\r\r\n- Written for the **audience's skill level**\r\r\n- Answers common questions preemptively\r\r\n- Troubleshooting section for known issues\r\r\n- Migration guides for breaking changes\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð Documentation Checklist\r\r\n\r\r\nBefore considering documentation complete, verify:\r\r\n\r\r\n- [ ] **Purpose is clear** in the first paragraph\r\r\n- [ ] **Installation steps** are tested and complete\r\r\n"]
[71.108427, "o", "- [ ] **Quick start** gets users t"]
[71.108484, "o", "o \"hello world\" fast\r\r\n- [ ] **Examples** cover common use cases\r\r\n- [ ] **API reference** is complete and accurate\r\r\n- [ ] **Error messages** are documented\r\r\n- [ ] **Links** are valid and point to current versions\r\r\n- [ ] **Code samples** are tested and working\r\r\n- [ ] **Formatting** is consistent throughout\r\r\n- [ ] **Navigation** is intuitive\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð¨ Formatting Standards\r\r\n\r\r\n### **Markdown Best Practices**\r\r\n- Use `#` hierarchies properly (don't skip levels)\r\r\n- Code blocks with language tags for syntax highlighting\r\r\n- Lists for scannable content\r\r\n- Tables for structured comparisons\r\r\n- Emojis sparingly for visual anchors (optional)\r\r\n- Bold for **emphasis**, italics for *terms*, code for `literals`\r\r\n\r\r\n### **Code Examples**\r\r\n```go\r\r\n// Good example structure:\r\r\n// 1. Context comment\r\r\n// 2. Minimal setup\r\r\n// 3. The actual usage\r\r\n// 4. Error handling\r\r\n\r\r\nctx := context.Background()\r\r\nclient, err := NewClient(ctx, \"api-key\")\r\r\nif err != nil {\r\r\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"client init: %w\", err)\r"]
[71.108488, "o", "\r\n}\r\r\ndefer client.Close()\r\r\n\r\r\nresult"]
[71.108547, "o", ", err := client.FetchData(ctx, \"query\")\r\r\nif err != nil {\r\r\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"fetch failed: %w\", err)\r\r\n}\r\r\n```\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð« Common Pitfalls to Avoid\r\r\n\r\r\n- **Outdated examples** that don't match current API\r\r\n- **Assumptions about user knowledge** without clarification\r\r\n- **Missing error handling** in examples\r\r\n- **Walls of text** without structure\r\r\n- **Vague descriptions** like \"handles the data\"\r\r\n- **Dead links** to external resources\r\r\n- **Copy-paste errors** between similar sections\r\r\n- **No version information** for breaking changes\r\r\n\r\r\n## ð Documentation as Code\r\r\n\r\r\n- Store in version control alongside code\r\r\n- Review in pull requests\r\r\n- Automate validation (link checking, code sample testing)\r\r\n- Treat documentation bugs as seriously as code bugs\r\r\n- Update documentation **in the same commit** as code changes\r\r\n\r\r\n---\r\r\n\r\r\n**Remember**: Good documentation is **discoverable**, **accurate**, **current**, and **helpful**. If users repeatedly ask the same questions, your documentati"]
[71.108553, "o", "on has gaps. Use those questions to"]
[71.108601, "o", " improve it continuously.\r\r\n"]
